{"name":"Irradiant Iris","hex":"#dadee6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"irradiant","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["That radiates light"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/irradiant"},{"term":"iris","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the genus Iris, common in the northern hemisphere, and generally having attractive blooms (See  Iris (plant) on  Wikipedia.Wikipedia ).","The contractile membrane perforated by the pupil, which adjusts to control the amount of light reaching the retina, and which forms the colored portion of the eye (See  Iris (anatomy) on  Wikipedia.Wikipedia )."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To open or close in the manner of an iris.","To cause (something) to shine with the colours of the rainbow; to make iridescent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/iris"}],"entries":[{"title":"Irradiant (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Irradiant is the third album by the French technical death metal band Scarve. This is the last album to feature Guillaume Bideau's vocals as he joined the Danish industrial metal band Mnemic in October 2006. The digipak version of the album includes two live bonus tracks \"Heaven-Sent\" and \"Luminiferous\", two video clips; \"Mirthless Perspectives\" and \"Emulate the Soul\" as well as an extended CD-ROM feature."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/38/Irradiant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irradiant_(album)","wikidata":"Q6073512"},{"title":"Iris (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Iris is an ambiguous color term, usually referring to shades ranging from blue-violet to violet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Unidentified_Iris_Chanticleer_Purple_2868px.jpg/330px-Unidentified_Iris_Chanticleer_Purple_2868px.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.